## Task Status Lifecycle

```
┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐
│  PENDING  │───►│ ASSIGNED │───►│ AWAITING_QA  │───►│ COMPLETED│───►│ ARCHIVED │
└──────────┘    └──────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────┘    └──────────┘
                      │                                  ▲
                      │                                  │
                      ▼                                  │
                 ┌──────────┐                           │
                 │ IN_PROGRESS│──────────────────────────┘
                 └──────────┘     (worker self-report)
                      │
                      ▼
                 ┌──────────┐
                 │ NEEDS_FIXES│
                 └──────────┘
                      │
                      └──────────► (reassign to worker)
```

## Workflow Documentation Standards

All workflow documents follow the template structure defined in [`_template.md`](_template.md):

- YAML frontmatter with metadata
- Role card with primary/cannot/work info
- Overview diagram (ASCII art)
- Decision framework (state transitions)
- Startup sequence
- Task/Asset type to skill mapping
- Workflow flow (detailed step-by-step)
- Sub-agents reference
- Skills reference
- Commit format
- Mandatory pre-commit checklist
- Exit conditions
- File permissions
- Messages you send/receive
- See Also cross-references

## Contributing

When adding new agents or modifying existing workflows:

1. Follow the [`_template.md`](_template.md) structure
2. Include all 15 required sections
3. Use proper YAML frontmatter
4. Create ASCII diagrams with box characters (─ │ ┌ ┐ └ ┘ ├ ┤ ┼)
5. Cross-reference related workflows in See Also section
6. Update this index with new workflow links

